    narr:generatedFrom "6554c93c5c55a181b729ea30886d1ffe6558631d" ;
    narr:narration """Xavier's turns in this session move between [inviting scrutiny of his own read before it lands elsewhere](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_10) and building out two separate technical positions. He opens with [a coupling argument for two sites sharing a desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), gets [agreement on the framing](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_14), then flags that [the evidence behind it is thin — one site, one season](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_21). He cites [a past cutover outage](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_24) to justify [a hard rule that reporting never touches the live system during cutover](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_26), then quantifies the tradeoff with [a replica-lag figure](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_28). A second, separate thread runs from [an open question on who owns reference data](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_34) to [a firm position that the vendor stays system of record until the last site is live](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_36), backed by [a drift-risk argument for keeping one source of truth](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_38).""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_10> ;
